{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram-", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "NMR", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals that the sequence of the peptide shows 88% similarity to Ocellatin-F1. molecular formula: C97H169N27O28S1; Mol Wt: 2193.632; GRAVY = 0.65. Activity: Weakly active against Gram- A.actinomycetemcomitans (MIC 222.37 uM), E.coli (MIC 114 uM). Its activity against Gram+ bacteria and fungi >200 uM. Structure: Structures were determined by NMR in DPC or SDS ( Gomes et al., 2018). You can rotate, zoom, and view the 3D structure here in the PDB. Updated 12/2019; 7/2021", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "28338958", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "J Venom Anim Toxins Incl Trop Dis. 2017 Jan 19;23:4. doi: 10.1186/s40409-017-0094-y. PubMed", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP02971", "source_id": "AP02971", "source_numeric_id": "02971", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP02971", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Ocellatin peptides from the skin secretion of the South American frog Leptodactylus labyrinthicus (Leptodactylidae): characterization, antimicrobial activities and membrane interactions.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
